❯ how do i exactly get an api key for metabrainz?

You most likely want the ListenBrainz user token. It's the one that unlocks the popularity endpoints that returned 401 earlier. MetaBrainz runs MusicBrainz, ListenBrainz and others, and one MetaBrainz account covers them all.

1. Account: go to https://musicbrainz.org/register to create a free MetaBrainz account, or skip this if you already have one.
2. Log in: go to https://listenbrainz.org and sign in with that account.
3. Token: open your profile menu, then Settings, or go straight to https://listenbrainz.org/settings/. There is a User token section with a copy button.
4. Store it: run vault set LISTENBRAINZ_TOKEN and paste it when prompted. If you're typing it into this session, use ! vault set LISTENBRAINZ_TOKEN.

I'm going from memory on where the settings page puts the token. If the layout has changed, look for "User token" there.

You don't need any other keys. MusicBrainz takes no key, and AcoustID is the separate one you already set up. Once the token is in vault, tell me and I'll check the real response from the top-recordings endpoint and add per-artist track suggestions to suggest.
